      "text": "Step 1: Identify the foci of the hyperbola. Given \\( F_1 = (10, 2) \\) and \\( F_2 = (-16, 2) \\), the center of the hyperbola is the midpoint of the segment joining the foci. Thus, the center \\( (h, k) \\) is calculated as follows:\n\\[ h = \\frac{10 + (-16)}{2} = \\frac{-6}{2} = -3 \\]\n\\[ k = \\frac{2 + 2}{2} = 2 \\]\nSo, the center of the hyperbola is \\( (-3, 2) \\).",
